  "code_findings": [
    "PARAM reads only report the requested controller field. eStop/recompute/reset occurs only inside the successful parameter-write branch.",
    "configured_rail is consumed for CENTER and successful HOME completion. It does not alter the negative seek rate.",
    "SEEK_NEG still requests -0.03m/s. With26666.6667steps/m this is800 commanded pulses/s; the timer interval is7us.",
    "ax_pos changes only in the ISR overflow branch that also writes D2 HIGH. Telemetry x is (ax_pos-home_steps)/steps_per_m, not integrated requested velocity.",
    "A -0.1539m reported change corresponds to approximately4104 attempted STEP writes. It is not independent physical displacement measurement.",
    "GPIO initialization keeps STEP/DIR atD2/D3 and shared active-low enable atD8. LCD and encoder pin assignments do not overlap. No microstep GPIO writes exist despite an inherited misleading comment.",
    "The instantaneous30mm/s homing start predates the parameter/home750 build; this audit does not validate motor pull-in torque or physical tracking."
  ],
  "conclusion": {
    "software_regression": "No new persistent pulse-generation defect was found in the parameter/home750 changes. Exact build comparison substantially weakens that specific explanation for the reported jitter/no-motion observation.",
    "not_proven": "The audit does not prove STEP, DIR or ENABLE electrical levels at the driver, pulse timing under actual hardware interrupt conditions, motor coil health, power/current, driver condition, coupling, belt motion, or mechanical freedom. The software step counter cannot establish motor following.",
    "discriminating_measurement": "Measure D2 STEP, D3 DIR and D8 ENABLE at the driver input during a separately authorized bounded test to distinguish electrical delivery from motor/driver/mechanical failure."
  }
